{% block requirements %}
## SPEC-Specific Requirements

### Structure Requirements
1. Specification Overview
2. Data Models (SPEC.DM.XX)
3. API Definitions (SPEC.API.XX)
4. Component Design (SPEC.CMP.XX)
5. Sequence Diagrams (SPEC.SEQ.XX)
6. Error Handling (SPEC.ERR.XX)
7. Configuration (SPEC.CFG.XX)

### Specification Categories
- **Data Models (DM)**: Entity definitions, relationships
- **API (API)**: Endpoint specs, payloads
- **Component (CMP)**: Module designs
- **Sequence (SEQ)**: Interaction flows
- **Error (ERR)**: Error codes, handling
- **Config (CFG)**: Configuration schemas

### Content Quality
- Implementation-ready detail
- Code examples included
- Edge cases documented
- Error scenarios covered
- Performance considerations

### ID Pattern
- Format: `SPEC.{TYPE}.XX` where TYPE is category
- Example: `SPEC.API.05` (API specification, fifth endpoint)

### Specification Format
```yaml
SPEC.API.XX:
  name: [API Name]
  method: GET|POST|PUT|DELETE
  path: /api/v1/resource
  description: |
    [Endpoint purpose]
  request:
    headers:
      Authorization: Bearer {token}
    query:
      page:
        type: integer
        default: 1
    body:
      schema: $ref CTR.SCH.XX
  response:
    200:
      schema: $ref CTR.SCH.YY
    400:
      schema: $ref SPEC.ERR.01
  trace:
    upstream: REQ.XX.YY
    contract: CTR.API.ZZ
```

### Traceability
- @trace: REQ.XX.YY (atomic requirements)
- @trace: CTR.XX (data contracts)
- Forward references to TSPEC
